# Netlify rules (see README.md). Another host ignores this file, or wants the "!" and the lines with a domain removed.
#
# The README is for the owner, not for visitors. "!" makes the rule win over the file that exists at this path.
/README.md  /  302!

# myrestring.com is the domain of the app's mail and API; whoever types it into a browser lands on the site. For this the
# domain has to be added to the Netlify project as a domain alias, with its DNS pointing at Netlify. http and https are
# separate rules.
http://myrestring.com/*  https://tryrestring.com/:splat  301!
https://myrestring.com/*  https://tryrestring.com/:splat  301!
http://www.myrestring.com/*  https://tryrestring.com/:splat  301!
https://www.myrestring.com/*  https://tryrestring.com/:splat  301!
